cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or model, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Oil Palm Crown Detection & Counting from UAV RGB Orthomosaics"
abstract: >-
  A YOLOv8s single-class detector and geospatial pipeline that detects and counts individual
  oil palms in drone RGB orthomosaics and produces a GIS-ready palm inventory. Trained on
  4,041 hand-labelled crowns; on held-out test tiles it reaches precision 0.845 and recall
  0.774, and its tile-interior palm count is within 0.2% of the hand count. Used in
  production to count 718,751 palms over 12,166.6 ha in West Africa. Includes an in-browser
  demo that runs the model on the user's own computer.
